Classic camera public-driver lifecycle fixture
=============================================

Files in this directory: shared bootloader/bootloader.bin,
shared partition_table/partition-table.bin, lifecycle.bin.
Source and pinned rebuild recipe: examples/classic-camera/lifecycle.md.

Linked application code is the simulator-owned MIT fixture, ESP-IDF v5.4.3
and esp32-camera b817e9b81041980608d1a3d3e0b08d86e3666382 (Apache-2.0),
Mbed TLS SHA-256 (Apache-2.0), FreeRTOS (MIT), TLSF (BSD-3-Clause),
Xtensa HAL (MIT), newlib (per-file licences), and GCC runtime
(GPLv3 with GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1).
The bootloader contains the same applicable ESP-IDF/runtime components.

Full third-party licence texts are at the repository-root path
web/wasm/fw/public/classic-hello-NOTICE.txt (ESP-IDF, Mbed TLS, FreeRTOS, newlib, GCC runtime,
TLSF and Xtensa HAL). The MIT application licence is the repository LICENSE.
The Apache-2.0 text there also applies to esp32-camera, Copyright Espressif
Systems (Shanghai) CO LTD. esp32-camera source is unchanged.

Inventory checked from the application and bootloader link maps, archive
members included to satisfy references. esp_phy contributes initialization
glue only: no Wi-Fi/Bluetooth controller archive is linked. esp_jpeg 1.3.1
is a pinned build dependency, but its decoder is not linked into these
RGB565/SHA-256 images. No JPEG runtime licence is claimed for this fixture.
No ROM ELF is redistributed here; tools/fetch-rom-elfs.sh fetches it separately.
